    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Notification Channels Test\n\nSend a test message to all configured notification channels.\n\n**Nodes requiring n8n Credentials** (configure in Settings → Credentials):\n- **Telegram** → create a `Telegram Bot` credential with your bot token\n- **WhatsApp (Twilio)** → create a `Twilio` credential with Account SID + Auth Token\n- **Send Email** → create an `SMTP` credential, then replace `REPLACE_WITH_SMTP_CREDENTIAL_ID`\n\nAfter creating the credentials, open each node and re-select the credential from the dropdown — this updates the internal ID.\n\n**All other nodes** read tokens/URLs directly from env vars. See `.env-example` for the full list.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "16cc9cbb-b985-45aa-b64e-478d9aa184a2",
      "name": "Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1184,
        784
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Dream Log Analyzer\n\nSend a voice note describing your dream. Every 7 entries, Ollama finds recurring themes and patterns.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Voice note → Whisper transcription\n2. Entry appended to `dreams.json` with date + time\n3. Every 7th dream → Ollama writes a pattern analysis\n4. Reply: \"Dream #N logged\" or full analysis\n\n**Dreams file:** `N8N_DATA_PATH/dreams.json`\nMake sure that path is writable from inside the n8n Docker container.\n\n**Setup:**\n- Create a `Telegram Bot` credential and replace `REPLACE_WITH_TELEGRAM_CREDENTIAL_ID`\n- Set `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `WHISPER_URL`, `WHISPER_MODEL`, `N8N_DATA_PATH` in `.env`\n- Run a Whisper-compatible server (speaches, faster-whisper-server, or use OpenAI)",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "bc9800a3-1cc4-49b9-aad4-02699e7d956a",
      "name": "Notes1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -400,
        1760
      ]
    }
